  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Japanese 1976-1986 sophisticated urban-adult-pop genre fusing late-1970s American AOR (adult-oriented rock), funk, fusion-jazz, and disco-soul into a distinct Tokyo-bubble-era mature-pop aesthetic. The instrumentation features electric-piano (Rhodes-and-Wurlitzer), fretless-bass, clean-electric-guitar (often with chorus pedal), brass section (often Roland JX-3P synth-brass), and breathy-intimate close-miked vocal-style. Lyrically focused on urban-leisure: nighttime-driving, summer-resort-and-beach, romantic-rendezvous-in-cafes-and-bars, and Tokyo-Yokohama-Shōnan coastal lifestyle. Originally a quiet commercial-niche aimed at the Japanese middle-class consumer-boom audience, city-pop gained massive 2010s-onward Western internet-re-discovery via vaporwave and YouTube-algorithmic-suggestion.",
